<p>
  Dear GitHub customer,
</p>

<% if @is_iap %>
<p>
  As you qualify for free access to GitHub Copilot Pro, your subscription benefits will now come at no cost.
  However, since you subscribed through an in-app purchase, you'll need to cancel your existing subscription
  manually to avoid future charges.
</p>

<p>
  <b>To cancel your subscription:</b>
</p>

<% if @is_google_iap %>
<p>
  <b>For Google Play Store subscriptions:</b><br>
  1. Go to Google Play Store > Menu > Subscriptions<br>
  2. Find and select your GitHub Copilot subscription<br>
  3. Tap "Cancel Subscription"<br>
  <br>
  <b>For refunds:</b> GitHub support can issue refunds for Google Play Store subscriptions. 
  Please contact our support team at <%= link_to "https://support.github.com/contact", "https://support.github.com/contact" %> 
  if you'd like to request a refund for any unused portion of your subscription.
</p>
<% else %>
<p>
  <b>For Apple App Store subscriptions:</b><br>
  1. Go to Settings > [Your Name] > Subscriptions on your iOS device<br>
  2. Find and select your GitHub Copilot subscription<br>
  3. Tap "Cancel Subscription"<br>
  <br>
  <b>For refunds:</b> Apple does not allow GitHub to issue refunds for App Store subscriptions. 
  To request a refund, you must reach out to Apple directly at <%= link_to "https://reportaproblem.apple.com", "https://reportaproblem.apple.com" %>.
</p>
<% end %>

<p>
  No other steps are needed to receive your free access to GitHub Copilot Pro!
</p>

<% else %>
<p>
  As you qualify for free access to GitHub Copilot Pro, we recently sent you a refund receipt for your subscription.
  No other steps are needed to receive your free access to GitHub Copilot Pro!
</p>

<p>
  <b>
    Note: It may take up to 14 days for the refund to be processed by your payment provider.
  </b>
</p>
<% end %>

<p>
  If you have any questions about your account, please contact support at:
  <%= link_to "https://support.github.com/contact", "https://support.github.com/contact" %>.
</p>
